; A four-wheeled VehicleBody3D, for the ONE variable no other golden moves: the
; VehicleWheel3D gizmo. Godot draws it for every wheel always (its
; vehicle_body_3d_gizmo_plugin: a radius circle in the YZ plane, a four-section
; spring coil, a travel line up to wheel_rest_length, axle ticks, and a forward
; arrow); we gate it on selection per ADR-0018, so only the `select:` golden
; captures it. No other fixture in the repo contains any of that geometry, which
; is why a regression in it would otherwise be invisible.
;
; Nothing else here is new: VehicleBody3D and VehicleWheel3D both render as
; transform-only groups (ADR-0005/0008), exactly like unit-rigidbody3d.tscn, so an
; unselected GOLDEN of this scene would move zero variables and none is
; registered. (The comparison sheets still capture the scene unselected — that
; pair exists to show the two engines agreeing, not to localise a regression.)
; `visible = false` on a fallback-bound type is likewise already pinned by
; unit-csg-combiner.tscn's golden.
;
; Wheel4 carries a larger wheel_radius and Wheel1 an explicit wheel_rest_length,
; so the gizmo's two size inputs are both exercised rather than left at defaults.
;
; What the golden actually shows of the gizmo is the radius circle and the
; forward arrow: the spring coil is wound at 0.2 × radius around the suspension
; axis, which puts it inside the wheel mesh, and the gizmo depth-tests (as
; Godot's does), so the coil and travel line are occluded. Their geometry is
; pinned numerically in Component.test.tsx instead — the golden is not the only
; cover for them.
